#: src/signing-in-to-gitlab.md:45
msgid "Logging-In in Android"
msgstr ""

#: src/signing-in-to-gitlab.md:47 src/signing-in-to-gitlab.md:57
msgid "Here are the steps:"
msgstr ""

#: src/signing-in-to-gitlab.md:48 src/signing-in-to-gitlab.md:58
msgid ""
"From your computer web browser, open the [Redox GitLab](https://gitlab.redox-"
"os.org/redox-os/)"
msgstr ""

#: src/signing-in-to-gitlab.md:49 src/signing-in-to-gitlab.md:59
msgid "Click the Sign In button"
msgstr ""

#: src/signing-in-to-gitlab.md:50 src/signing-in-to-gitlab.md:60
msgid "Enter your username/email"
msgstr ""

#: src/signing-in-to-gitlab.md:51 src/signing-in-to-gitlab.md:61
msgid "Enter your password"
msgstr ""

#: src/signing-in-to-gitlab.md:52 src/signing-in-to-gitlab.md:62
msgid "Click the Submit button"
msgstr ""

#: src/signing-in-to-gitlab.md:53
msgid ""
"Finally you will be prompted for a 2FA verification code from your phone. Go "
"to your Android phone, go to Google/Aegis Authenticator, find the site "
"gitlab redox and underneith those 6 digits in looking something like **258 "
"687** that's your 2FA code.  Enter those 6 digits into the prompt on your "
"computer.  Click Verify.  Done.  You're logged into Gitlab."
msgstr ""

#: src/signing-in-to-gitlab.md:55
msgid "Logging-In in iOS"
msgstr ""

#: src/signing-in-to-gitlab.md:63
msgid ""
"Finally you will be prompted for a 2FA verification code from your phone. Go "
"to your iPhone, go to 2stable/Tofu Authenticator or to your Settings-"
">Passwords for iOS Authenticator, find the site gitlab redox and underneath "
"those 6 digits in looking something like **258 687** that's your 2FA code.  "
"Enter those 6 digits into the prompt on your computer.  Click Verify.  "
"Done.  You're logged into Gitlab."
msgstr ""

#: src/signing-in-to-gitlab.md:65
msgid "Setting up PAT"
msgstr ""

#: src/signing-in-to-gitlab.md:67
msgid ""
"Personal Access Token (PAT) is a replacement for passwords when "
"authenticating via Git clients. When pushing code to GitLab, you need to "
"create one."
msgstr ""

#: src/signing-in-to-gitlab.md:69
msgid "Here are the steps needed to create a PAT after logging in to GitLab:"
msgstr ""

#: src/signing-in-to-gitlab.md:70
msgid ""
"Open [Personal access tokens in User settings](https://gitlab.redox-os.org/-/"
"user_settings/personal_access_tokens)"
msgstr ""

#: src/signing-in-to-gitlab.md:71
msgid ""
"Click \"Generate Token\" at the top right of the \"Personal access tokens\" "
"section, and select \"Legacy token\""
msgstr ""

#: src/signing-in-to-gitlab.md:72
msgid ""
"Enter the token name (can be anything) and expiration date (max is 1 year "
"from today)"
msgstr ""

#: src/signing-in-to-gitlab.md:73
msgid "Check `read_repository` and `write_repository` scopes"
msgstr ""

#: src/signing-in-to-gitlab.md:74
msgid "Click \"Generate Token\""
msgstr ""

#: src/signing-in-to-gitlab.md:75
msgid ""
"Copy the PAT (displayed as masked password) under the section \"Token "
"details\""
msgstr ""

#: src/signing-in-to-gitlab.md:76
msgid "Save the PAT somewhere safe, like your password manager"
msgstr ""

#: src/signing-in-to-gitlab.md:78
msgid ""
"When doing `git push`, you'll be asked for username and password. Enter the "
"password from the PAT token you've created. This will happen every time you "
"run `git push`. To remember it forever, run the command below to store it "
"later in `~/.git-credentials`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/signing-in-to-gitlab.md:84
msgid ""
"If you don't like to store it as plain text, it's also possible to save it "
"only in RAM cache:"
msgstr ""

#: src/signing-in-to-gitlab.md:87
msgid ""
"# <timeout> is how long it will be preserved in memory, defaults to 900 "
"(seconds)\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/signing-in-to-gitlab.md:88
msgid "'cache --timeout=<timeout>'"
msgstr ""

#: src/signing-in-to-gitlab.md:91
msgid "If you have lost your PAT, it's OK to create another one."
msgstr ""
